  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "8d110fe0-bead-9f75-4885-97bc4a76739e",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "cc480366-1531-a068-3cff-0dd0c5dd4d98",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Through the Hazara oral and written poetry that she aims to collect, transcribe and translate, Shukria will be bringing attention to the plight and the challenges faced by Hazara community in Afghanistan. This project is not only a celebration of Hazaragi poetry but also a way of documenting Hazara's history and plight by making it accessible to non-Hazaras.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "attrs": {
                "level": 4
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Shukria Rezaei ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "A Hazara from Afghanistan who has been living in the UK for the last 10 years. Her journey in writing poetry began in her school years. She is now a graduate of BA Philosophy, Politics & Economics, and MSc Human Rights & Politics. She has written poems primarily on her journey of seeking sanctuary and the genocide of her people - the Hazaras. Through her poetry, she has advocated for the rights of her people. Now, she is launching her own blog where she collects, transcribes and translates Hazaragi poems into English.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
